arts still changing at loop 24 (UNSETTLED), 0 settled on a wrong grid (STUCK).", "<b>float32 is touchy.</b> Re-run on a second float32 implementation, 97% of the pixels with flat surroundings keep their settle time but only 26% of the speckle pixels do. On the same GPU, a nudge of 1e-6 to a start leaves 97% of flat-region pixels unchanged and 18% of speckle pixels. (Ours vs loopscape's published image: 64.4% of 62,500 pixels identical.) TF32 or bfloat16 give a different picture. Read single speckle pixels as one realisation; the structure is the result.", "<b>The complexity thins out when you zoom.</b> In 5\u00d75-pixel boxes, 69% touch a boundary at the full map's pixel pitch (1e-03), but only 31% in the layer magnified \u00d7128 (pitch 3e-05). Zoom beyond \u00d7128 was not rendered: a trial window at \u00d75,120 held only speckle next to a flat domain.", "<b>Settle time</b> is measured over 24 loops with the model's noise switched off, as in loopscape: the loop after which the decoded grid never changes again."], "how": ["EqR checkpoint (locuslab) run as in loopscape: z_H = a\u00b7u + b\u00b7v, z_L = 0, 24 loops, noise off, float32.", "6,016,804 starting thoughts computed on A100 GPUs of the ALICE cluster (Leiden): 2048\u00b2 for the full plane and 5 zoom layers around the marked point. About 25 A100-hours.", "A start stops being computed once its decoded grid has equalled the true solution for 3 loops in a row (checked against full 24-loop runs).", "Reproduction check: loopscape's published 1000\u00d71000 image, every 4th pixel: basin entropy 1.416 vs 1.412, boundary dimension 1.873 vs 1.872."], "reproduce": {"flat": 0.969187675070028, "edge": 0.6555555555555556, "dust": 0.25906735751295334}, "featured": [{"id": "fast", "label": "a quick thought", "title": "settles in 3 loops", "layer": 0, "col": 1964, "row": 818, "zoom": 6, "settle": 3, "solved": true, "trace": ["236354791974325683891697452769535824583462967142789563327916245498278316618543279", "236154798971328